    "text": "\u00d0is is seo ger\u00e6dnys, \u00fee Eadgar cyng mid his witena ge\u00f0eahte ger\u00e6dde, Gode to lofe & him sylfum to\n\u00de\u00e6t syndon \u00feonne \u00e6rest, \u00fe\u00e6t Godes cyrican syn rihtes wyr\u00f0e.\n& man agife \u00e6lce teo\u00f0unge to \u00feam ealdan mynstre, \u00fee seo hernes tohyr\u00f0; & \u00fe\u00e6t sy \u00feonne swa gel\u00e6st,\nGyf hwa \u00feonne \u00f0egna sy, \u00f0e on his boclande cyrican habbe, \u00fee legerstow on sy, gesylle he \u00feane \u00feriddan\nGyf hwa cyrican habbe, \u00fee legerstow on ne sie, \u00f0onne do he of \u00feam nigan d\u00e6lum his preoste \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6t\n& ga \u00e6lc cyricsceat into \u00feam ealdan mynstre be \u00e6lcum frigan eor\u00f0e.\n& sie \u00e6lcre geogu\u00f0e teo\u00f0ung gel\u00e6st be pentecosten & \u00feara eor\u00f0w\u00e6stma be emnihte; & \u00e6lc cyricsceat sy\n& gyf hwa \u00feonne \u00f0a teo\u00f0unge gel\u00e6stan nelle, swa we gecwedan habba\u00f0, fare \u00fe\u00e6s cynges gerefa to &\n& tod\u00e6le man \u00fea eahta d\u00e6las on twa, & fo se landhlaford to ealfan, to ealfan se biscop, sy hit cynges\n& sy \u00e6lc heor\u00f0p\u00e6ning agyfen be Petres m\u00e6ssed\u00e6g.\n& se \u00f0e \u00feonne to \u00f0am andagan gel\u00e6st n\u00e6bbe, l\u00e6de hine to Rome & \u00fe\u00e6rto eacan XXX p\u00e6nega, &\n& gyf he hine eft syllan nylle, l\u00e6de hine eft to Rome & o\u00f0re swylce bote; & \u00feonne he ham cume, gylde\n\u00c6t \u00feam \u00feriddan cyrre gyf he \u00feonne git nelle, \u00feolie ealles \u00fe\u00e6s \u00f0e he age.\n& healde man \u00e6lces Sunnand\u00e6ges freols fram nontide \u00fe\u00e6s S\u00e6ternesd\u00e6ges o\u00f0 \u00f0\u00e6s Monand\u00e6ges lihtinge,\n& man beboden f\u00e6sten healde mid \u00e6lcre geornfulnesse.",
